How Hamnix Micro uses them: as DATA.  Nothing here is compiled or linked into an
image.  Hamnix Micro's drivers are Adder (soc/imxrt/, soc/imxrt1062/,
boards/teensy41/); the scripts in tests/imxrt/ read these files as text and
check every register address, offset, bit mask, interrupt number, pin-mux
tuple and clock gate the Adder code uses against them, and check the boot
header against the structures defined here.

